  "note": "First election under proportional representation. Uncontested by agreement between the parties: the Unionists rose from six members to eight, the Nationalists fell from twelve to five, and Sinn Féin won its first seats. Occupations printed in the source are not recorded. P. J. M'Garvey was a member of the old council."
